"Anubis spends 106 us of CPU per admitted request in forward-auth mode, "
"where Sibuna spends 13; its peak resident memory was about 32 MiB in "
"forward-auth mode and grew to about 600 MiB in reverse-proxy mode, while "
"Sibuna's stayed near 16 MiB throughout. Behind ``caddy respond`` Sibuna's "
"proxied rows are limited by the origin, which shares the load generator's "
"CPUs: with the lighter stub origin of :ref:`whole-products` the same rows "
"reach about 139,000 requests per second."
msgstr ""
